node_modules/
dist/
.llamacli/state/
# Per-machine runtime config. The bootstrap (src/setup/) rewrites this on every
# launch with values derived from the local GPU/VRAM/RAM — gpuLayers, threads,
# contextSize, laya.port — so it is a property of the BOX, not of the project,
# and committing it makes every user's machine share one machine's tuning.
# `.llamacli/rules/` stays tracked: those are meant to be shared.
.llamacli/config.yaml
# Config backups written next to it by whichever session last rewrote it. They
# capture one machine's endpoint/model, same as the config itself.
.llamacli/*.bak*
*.log
.claude/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Scratch verification harnesses. These are throwaway scripts used to prove a
# single behaviour against a real payload (e.g. checking the pure-Node tar
# extractor against GNU long names) — the assertions that matter are in the real
# test suite, not in a copy of the logic pasted into a standalone file where it
# can drift from src/ and rot.
tmp_*.mjs
tmp_*/
test/containers/results/
